You are supporting a process mining research prototype.
Use only the synthetic scenario information provided below.
Do not invent company-specific system names, product names, confidential logs, internal metrics, or real organizational details.
Return valid JSON only. Do not wrap it in Markdown.

Scenario ID: S05
Scenario title: Specification Document Review
Initial workflow description:
An engineer reviews a specification document to check whether new features are reflected correctly and whether there are typos or missing details.

Clarification questions:
[
  {
    "id": "Q1",
    "question": "What event or condition triggers the engineer to begin reviewing a specification document — for example, a notification from a document management system, a new version being published, or a manual request?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q2",
    "question": "In which system or location does the specification document live, and how does the engineer access the version that needs to be reviewed?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q3",
    "question": "Does the engineer follow a defined checklist or set of criteria when reviewing the document, and if so, what are the main items on that list?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q4",
    "question": "What are the possible outcomes at the end of the review, and what action does the engineer take for each outcome — for example, approving the document, requesting changes, or escalating to someone else?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q5",
    "question": "How does the engineer record and communicate review findings — for instance, through inline comments in the document, a separate feedback form, a tracking ticket, or an email?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q6",
    "question": "Is the review performed solely by one engineer, or do other roles participate, and is there a defined process if reviewers disagree or if no response is received within a certain timeframe?"
  }
]
Reference workflow for oracle use:
{
  "goal": "Review a specification document for feature coverage, consistency, and editorial errors.",
  "actors": [
    "document reviewer",
    "feature owner",
    "document author",
    "approver"
  ],
  "systems": [
    "document repository",
    "change request tracker",
    "review checklist",
    "commenting tool"
  ],
  "inputs": [
    "specification document",
    "feature change list",
    "previous document version",
    "review checklist"
  ],
  "outputs": [
    "review comments",
    "change request list",
    "approval decision",
    "updated document"
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "id": "A1",
      "name": "Collect document and related change list",
      "actor": "document reviewer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A2",
      "name": "Compare feature changes with document content",
      "actor": "document reviewer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A3",
      "name": "Check terminology and formatting consistency",
      "actor": "document reviewer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A4",
      "name": "Record comments and requested revisions",
      "actor": "document reviewer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A5",
      "name": "Revise document based on comments",
      "actor": "document author"
    },
    {
      "id": "A6",
      "name": "Confirm revisions with feature owner",
      "actor": "feature owner"
    },
    {
      "id": "A7",
      "name": "Approve final document",
      "actor": "approver"
    }
  ],
  "decisions": [
    {
      "id": "D1",
      "condition": "Are all feature changes reflected?",
      "branches": [
        "complete",
        "missing changes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "D2",
      "condition": "Are the revisions acceptable?",
      "branches": [
        "approve",
        "request another revision"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "exceptions": [
    "missing change list",
    "conflicting terminology",
    "unclear feature owner",
    "unresolved comments"
  ],
  "dependencies": [
    {
      "from": "A1",
      "to": "A2",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A2",
      "to": "A3",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A3",
      "to": "A4",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A4",
      "to": "A5",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A5",
      "to": "A6",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A6",
      "to": "A7",
      "type": "control_flow"
    }
  ],
  "automation_opportunities": [
    {
      "target": "A2",
      "rationale": "Feature coverage can be checked by comparing change lists and document sections."
    },
    {
      "target": "A3",
      "rationale": "Terminology, formatting, and typo checks can be automated."
    },
    {
      "target": "A4",
      "rationale": "Review comments can be grouped by section, severity, and owner."
    }
  ]
}
Task: Simulate a concise domain expert who answers only these questions using the reference workflow.
Do not reveal the full reference workflow. Do not add details not needed by the questions.
If a requested fact is absent, explicitly say it is not specified; do not guess.
Use at most 80 words per answer. Return one answer for each question, with matching ID and question text.
Return JSON: {"answers": [{"question_id": "Q1", "question": "original question", "answer": "grounded answer"}]}

Additional constraint for this respondent: this expert knows only part of the process. Answer questions
Q1 through Q3 as instructed above. For every remaining question, reply exactly:
"I am not sure about that." Do not provide any fact for those questions.
